d $i^i$ Even Mean?#1.3 Feeding an imaginary input to the series — the spiral *(at [[02:32]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=152s))*#{1}":[39,43],"#i to the power i#1. The Puzzle: What Could $i^i$ Even Mean?#1.4 The circular trap: \"$x=\\ln i$\" gets us nowhere *(at [[03:38]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=218s))*":[44,55],"#i to the power i#1. The Puzzle: What Could $i^i$ Even Mean?#1.4 The circular trap: \"$x=\\ln i$\" gets us nowhere *(at [[03:38]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=218s))*#{1}":[46,55],"#i to the power i#2. Computing One Value: $i^i = e^{-\\pi/2}$":[56,84],"#i to the power i#2. Computing One Value: $i^i = e^{-\\pi/2}$#2.1 Solving $e^x = i$ with Euler's formula *(at [[04:31]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=271s))*":[58,65],"#i to the power i#2. Computing One Value: $i^i = e^{-\\pi/2}$#2.1 Solving $e^x = i$ with Euler's formula *(at [[04:31]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=271s))*#{1}":[60,65],"#i to the power i#2. Computing One Value: $i^i = e^{-\\pi/2}$#2.2 The substitution and the exponent rule *(at [[06:22]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=382s))*":[66,84],"#i to the power i#2. Computing One Value: $i^i = e^{-\\pi/2}$#2.2 The substitution and the exponent rule *(at [[06:22]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=382s))*#{1}":[68,84],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)":[85,123],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#{1}":[87,88],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.1 Position and velocity: $\\frac{d}{dt}e^{it} = i\\,e^{it}$ *(at [[09:50]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=590s))*":[89,96],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.1 Position and velocity: $\\frac{d}{dt}e^{it} = i\\,e^{it}$ *(at [[09:50]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=590s))*#{1}":[91,96],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.2 Velocity is the position rotated 90° → circular motion *(at [[10:12]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=612s))*":[97,106],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.2 Velocity is the position rotated 90° → circular motion *(at [[10:12]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=612s))*#{1}":[99,106],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.3 The walking quiz *(at [[11:26]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=686s))*":[107,114],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.3 The walking quiz *(at [[11:26]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=686s))*#{1}":[109,114],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.4 Reading $i$ as \"where you are after $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ of time\" *(at [[14:48]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=888s))*":[115,123],"#i to the power i#3. The Intuition: Why Does Euler's Formula Work? (Dynamics)#3.4 Reading $i$ as \"where you are after $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ of time\" *(at [[14:48]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=888s))*#{1}":[117,123],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$":[124,161],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.1 The three roles of $i$ in $i^i$ *(at [[15:08]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=908s))*":[126,135],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.1 The three roles of $i$ in $i^i$ *(at [[15:08]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=908s))*#{1}":[128,135],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.2 Raising to $i$ turns rotation into decay: $e^{it} \\to e^{-t}$ *(at [[15:30]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=930s))*":[136,152],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.2 Raising to $i$ turns rotation into decay: $e^{it} \\to e^{-t}$ *(at [[15:30]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=930s))*#{1}":[138,152],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.3 So $i^i$ is \"decay for $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ of time\" *(at [[18:15]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1095s))*":[153,161],"#i to the power i#4. The Dynamic Meaning of Raising to the Power $i$#4.3 So $i^i$ is \"decay for $\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}$ of time\" *(at [[18:15]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1095s))*#{1}":[155,161],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means":[162,219],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.1 What exponentiation actually is: $f(a+b)=f(a)\\,f(b)$ *(at [[21:56]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1316s))*":[164,179],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.1 What exponentiation actually is: $f(a+b)=f(a)\\,f(b)$ *(at [[21:56]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1316s))*#{1}":[166,179],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.2 Other solutions to $e^x=i$: winding around again *(at [[19:28]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1168s))*":[180,190],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.2 Other solutions to $e^x=i$: winding around again *(at [[19:28]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1168s))*#{1}":[182,190],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.3 The infinite ladder of values *(at [[24:13]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1453s))*":[191,210],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Really Means#5.3 The infinite ladder of values *(at [[24:13]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pq9LcwC7CoY&t=1453s))*#{1}":[193,210],"#i to the power i#5. Infinitely Many Values & What Exponentiation Reall